From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Reilly <packager@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Mar 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] data: add missing auth schema keys required by gnome-shell 49

gnome-shell 49.4 references enable-passkey-authentication,
enable-web-authentication, and enable-switchable-authentication from
org.gnome.login-screen GSettings schema in gdm/util.js
_updateAuthServices(). These keys were added to upstream GDM post-49.2
but are absent from the 49.2 tarball, causing gnome-shell to crash at
the GDM login screen with "GSettings key not found".
---
 data/org.gnome.login-screen.gschema.xml | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/data/org.gnome.login-screen.gschema.xml b/data/org.gnome.login-screen.gschema.xml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/data/org.gnome.login-screen.gschema.xml
+++ b/data/org.gnome.login-screen.gschema.xml
@@ -121,5 +121,20 @@
         giving up and going back to user selection.
       </description>
     </key>
+    <key name="enable-passkey-authentication" type="b">
+      <default>false</default>
+      <summary>Whether or not to allow passkey (FIDO2) authentication for login</summary>
+      <description>The login screen can optionally allow users to log in using FIDO2 passkey devices.</description>
+    </key>
+    <key name="enable-web-authentication" type="b">
+      <default>false</default>
+      <summary>Whether or not to allow web (WebAuthn) authentication for login</summary>
+      <description>The login screen can optionally allow web authentication.</description>
+    </key>
+    <key name="enable-switchable-authentication" type="b">
+      <default>false</default>
+      <summary>Whether or not to allow switching authentication methods</summary>
+      <description>The login screen can optionally allow switching between authentication methods.</description>
+    </key>
   </schema>
 </schemalist>
